Models downloaded at runtime (not distributed with this repository):
- mispeech/ced-base (CED, Apache-2.0), the default tagger; approximately 343 MB of weights
- MIT/ast-finetuned-audioset-10-10-0.4593 (Audio Spectrogram Transformer, BSD-3-Clause), optional; approximately 346 MB of weights
- laion/clap-htsat-unfused (LAION CLAP, Apache-2.0); approximately 615 MB of weights
Each is fetched from Hugging Face under its own licence on first use.
Sizes are rounded decimal MB from the locally cached checkpoints; configuration,
tokenizer files and Python dependencies are additional. CED plus CLAP need roughly 1 GB.
The default CED tagger pins its audited implementation to revision
db3e14a8db4c21b56b165261c39649741a900e7f. Models and their
configuration files remain in the user cache, under their respective licences.

Universal Category System (UCS) taxonomy:
- UCS v8.2.1, 753 subcategories in 82 categories, retrieved 12 October 2026
  from https://universalcategorysystem.com/ through its official resource link,
  https://resources.universalcategorysystem.com/.
- The official UCS homepage describes UCS as "a public domain initiative";
  it publishes no separate licence text. The list is reproduced on that basis.
  Attribution: Universal Category System, its creators and contributors
  (Tim Nielsen, Justin Drury, Kai Paquin and others).
- The bundled ucs_mapping.json preserves official category/subcategory names,
  CatIDs, category abbreviations, explanations and synonyms. The downloaded
  source spreadsheet SHA-256 is recorded in that file.
- One book synonym is excluded by the publication privacy filter; the normalized
  data records this omission and retains every category identity.
- AudioSet correspondences, legacy aliases and CLAP prompts are authored by
  Ultimate Audio Partner; they are not part of the official UCS list.
  Empty AudioSet mappings are explicitly unsupported, not invented labels.

AudioSet:
- CED and AST report the 527 AudioSet classes. Individual class names appear in
  this repository as identifiers for those model outputs.
- The AudioSet ontology is by Google LLC, licensed under Creative Commons
